<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35769" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννέᾰ</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		 also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννῆ</span></b>  (q.v.),
			indecl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>nine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.174
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.258
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοῦσαι ἐννέα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					917
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.60
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς ἐννέα κλῶνας,</span> in a
			religious ceremony, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				483
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς ἐ. ἔτη</span> Orac. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as a round
			number for, <i>many,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς ἐννέα φῶτας ἔπεφνεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.785
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.577
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				781
			</span></i>. (Cf. Lat. <i>novem,</i> Skt. <i>náva,</i>
			etc.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
